# Git Publish Rule

Before publishing, apply `.cursor/rules/delivery-batching.mdc`.

## Default

Do not create tiny standalone PRs or live deploys for every small edit.

Use one PR and one deploy per meaningful phase whenever safe.

## Publish Immediately Only When

| Case | Action |
|---|---|
| runtime behavior changed and the phase is complete | PR, CI, merge, deploy, live verification |
| production outage or CI blocker | small PR allowed |
| user explicitly asks to publish now | publish after verification |

## Bundle Instead When

| Case | Action |
|---|---|
| docs-only change | bundle with the next large phase |
| governance-only change | bundle unless it blocks CI or prevents regression |
| adjacent small cleanup | wait for the next scoped batch |

## Report

Every final report must state whether the change was:

- published now
- bundled for a later batch
- kept local pending the next phase
